y annoying and he  admitted to hating it expectations meet  reality  number 10 sometimes an actor just needs  to breathe like his co-stars sebastian  stan struggled with the heat he feared  falling over or passing out some days he  would rip his mask off his face just to  get a breath of fresh air flexibility  was a major issue so rehearsing out of  costume didn't translate once he got on  set but he's a pro and chose to wear the  least mobile arms because they looked  the coolest i always wanted to make it  tighter  number 11 back in the good old days  costumes were even worse they're much  more comfortable now than they were  before nobody knows how uncomfortable  those costumes are willem dafoe's  costume for no way home is more flexible  and he can do more in it there have been  upgrades on the costume let's say  originally to be fitted for the green  goblin costume it took them eight hours  of sticking pieces to him now he just  gets his body scanned and his job is  done  number 12 less cgi almost always makes a  movie better  jamie foxx is much happier to be his own  skin tone in spider-man no way home and  i didn't have to be blue and things like  that jamie didn't particularly hate  being blue but now he's thrilled to look  more like himself he felt like his old  costume was just trying too hard  number 13 just smile through the pain og  venom actor topher grace's fangs were  bruising his gums  and like many of the other superhero  actors he had no way to use the bathroom  in his costume either  number 14. from puppets to cgi alfred  molina may just be the exception in the  spider-verse he absolutely loved the  upgrades to doc ock being released from  the puppetry allowed him a lot more  freedom with the character and he loved  it like he absolutely loved it number 15  you may take his name but you will never  take his armor falcon and the winter  soldier actor wyatt russell who played  the new cap found his costume was like  the rest of the marvel gangs except tack  on painful the suit was so bad that he  had an old shoulder injury flare up  number 16 what's worse struggling to  breathe or not being able to scratch  that itch chadwick boseman's spandex  were tight and suffocating to get into  restricting his chest he suffered from  anxiety attacks when that happened he  had to get the suit off as quickly as  possible and there was sweat rolling  down his body that made him itchy and he  couldn't scratch  number 17. this reminds us of that old  wives tale about peeing in a public pool  rebecca romain's mystique costume is the  most revealing of all the marvel  characters  she was naked aside from paint and her  prosthetics which made her super  uncomfortable and going to the bathroom  was embarrassing because there was blue  paint on everything everybody knew when  she used the bathroom because the toilet  seat was blue  number 18 why didn't they design  mystique to have a bodysuit from the  beginning while romaine's eight hour  makeup process was streamlined for  jennifer lawrence down to around three  it still wasn't a fun process  and going to the bathroom was super  awkward for her too she revealed she  would have to pee out of a funnel  standing up  she joked that the designers thought she  doesn't go to the bathroom she's a girl  and jayla had such a negative reaction  to the blue paint that they had to call  a doctor to set  after that they gave her a bodysuit  instead  number 19. the suit broke the poor man  in the first iron man movie robert  downey jr wore a full metal suit that  weighed a hundred pounds rdj struggled  with breathing in the mask was blinded  by its led lights and the suit was  pinchy downey admitted i'm not  claustrophobic but after moving around  in it for a couple hours your spirit is  kind of broken and you're like okay time  to bring in the sun team number 20. this  actress liked her suit more than her  wellness eggs while rdj was struggling  with his metal suit gwyneth paltrow  loved every minute in hers  well she only spent a couple days in it  she would have gladly put the armor back  on yeah i was like don't we need another  scene or pepper's flying around  number 21 he got off lucky for a solid  second captain america's helmet gave  chris evans a headache it was tight  sweaty uncomfortable and made it hard to  hear while he didn't like his usual  costume he did really love his stealth  suit from the winter soldier he liked  that suit so much he kept pushing for  them to bring it back but the classic  red won out  number 22 he did not get off lucky at  all chris hemsworth has had a few not so  great experiences with costumes the  first is with the regular thor costume  by month 3 in the suit it gets hard to  wake up and put the thing on every  morning the fat suit was also terrible  the thing weighed about 60 to 70 pounds  before adding armor  and like every other suit it was  restrictive uncomfortable and super hot  number 23 you can't sit with us if you  don't have a cool suit  mark ruffalo just felt plain embarrassed  while all his other actor friends got to  wear cool looking suits all the time he  was just done up in a mocap suit he  never felt as cool or as intimidating as  the others  number 24 i'm melting i'm melting  dave bautista spent five hours in the  makeup chair he had to stand for most of  it with his arms sticking out and  rubbing the makeup off at the end of the  day was so tough on his body his skin  looked like hamburger meat he spent time  in the sauna to melt off the prosthetics  he and paul bettany aren't the only ones  to do so michael b jordan went through a  similar process to remove all those scar  marks  number 25 she's calling it like she sees  it  evangeline lily absolutely adores her  costume it makes her feel sexy  she thinks it's cool killer powerful  modern strong and it made me feel like a  superhero she also called out all the  men for complaining about their suits  she was surprised it wasn't so bad which  led her to question if men are just used  to feeling more comfortable in their  clothing while she wears heels to work  all day you get used to it you tune it  out that's 25 actors who had a lot of  feelings about their costumes  just let the actors complain okay every  time they walk into one of those  interview rooms it's the equivalent of  being asked hi honey how was your day  whose complaints surprised you the most  let us know in the comments thanks for  watching
 

